findings.body:
The Retry Jitter Factor cell now uses a truthiness check. A factor of `0` is a valid configured value, but it is falsy, so the sidebar shows "None" where the previous code showed `0`. That is a regression. The same pattern shows up in Cache Key and Dynamic Key, but those are strings where empty is a reasonable "None", so they are fine.

::diff{file="ui-v2/src/components/task-runs/task-run-details/task-run-details.tsx" lines="177-183"}

Use an explicit null/undefined check, the same way the Duration and Estimated Run Time fields already do.

The `StateType` union includes `CANCELLING` and `PAUSED`, and the hook builds the path as `/${stateType.toLowerCase()}.svg` for any truthy value. The PR only adds SVGs for cancelled, completed, crashed, failed, pending, running, and scheduled. For a CANCELLING or PAUSED run, the favicon `<link>` elements point to `/cancelling.svg` or `/paused.svg`, which return 404. The browser then shows a broken or blank tab icon. The checklist calls out that these states "will not update favicon", but the hook doesn't leave the default icon in place. It actively points at a missing file.

::diff{file="ui-v2/src/hooks/use-state-favicon.ts" lines="49-53"}

Either add the two SVGs, or only set the href when the state has an icon, so the default favicon stays in place.

The Flow Run branch now renders the link whenever `flow_run_id` is set, but the previous code required `flow_run_name` as well. If `flow_run_id` is present and `flow_run_name` is null, the link renders as an icon with no label. The breadcrumb in the header has the same condition, so that version would also be empty.

::diff{file="ui-v2/src/components/task-runs/task-run-details/task-run-details.tsx" lines="45-58"}

Falling back to the ID or to "None" for the label would avoid an unlabeled link.
